course: dictionary
lesson: 3065
title: A word about money
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An economist is a person who studies money, jobs, prices and trade. Economics is the subject they know well. Like a detective, an economist looks at clues and tries to explain why things happen.
explain: Look at the context. «In 1817 the economist David Ricardo explained that countries gain by doing what they do best and trading, like swapping spare stickers.» Ricardo is called an economist because he explained something about trade, which means swapping or buying and selling.
explain: The phrases «a leading economist» and «economists predict» give more clues. A leading economist is an important expert, and predict means say what will probably happen next.
explain: Economists do not always agree. «It was reported that prices rose very fast in many countries in 2022; economists disagree about the causes» shows that experts can hold different ideas. A good reader notices when some economists think one thing and others think another.
fact: An economist is a person who studies or is an expert in economics.
fact: Economics is about how money, jobs, prices and trade work.
fact: Economists often explain why prices go up and what may happen to jobs.
fact: «Economists predict» means economists say what they think will happen in the future.
fact: The plural of economist is economists: one economist, many economists.
exercise: What is an economist? | *A person who studies money, jobs, prices and trade | A person who designs ships | A person who sells fruit at a market | A person who looks after farm animals
exercise: «In 1817 the economist David Ricardo explained that countries gain by doing what they do best and trading.» What is the job of David Ricardo here? | *An expert on how money and trade work | A teacher of drawing | A ship's captain | A famous footballer
exercise: Find and copy the word that means more than one economist. | economy | predict | explain | *economists
test: «Economists predict» what does predict mean? | Count all the coins in a bank | Stop something from happening | Remember what happened in the past | *Say what will probably happen in the future
test: Why do economists sometimes disagree? | *Because experts can see the causes of things differently | Because they all work in the same office | Because money is not real | Because they never read any news
exam: Which sentence uses economist correctly? | Economist is a colour, like green or blue. | We bought an economist at the shop on Saturday. | The economist wrote a book about how trade works. | *The economist explained why prices rose, so she is an expert in economics.
